course: dictionary
lesson: 2568
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The words around the word show you which meaning the writer means. Read the whole sentence, then ask: which meaning fits here? Delivery is a good example.
explain: «We got a delivery this morning» means that something arrived, such as a parcel. «Texts about a parcel that could not be delivered» means a parcel was taken to a place, or was meant to be. The clues are parcels, drivers and goods.
explain: In cricket, a delivery is one ball bowled by the bowler. In the sentence about a flower, delivery means pollen travelling to the middle part of a flower. Check the topic first: parcels, a game, or a living thing.
explain: Swap your meaning into the sentence to test it. If the sentence still makes sense, you have found the right one.
fact: Delivery means taking letters, parcels or goods to the place they are sent to.
fact: A delivery can also be the thing that arrives: «We got a delivery.»
fact: In cricket, a delivery is one ball bowled.
fact: Delivery can also mean the birth of a baby.
fact: A delivery drone carries a small parcel along a planned route, using GPS, and lowers the parcel down.
exercise: «We got a delivery this morning.» In this sentence, what is a delivery? | A shop where letters are kept | The way someone speaks to an audience | The birth of a baby | *Something that has arrived, such as a parcel
exercise: In cricket, what is a delivery? | A parcel sent by post | *One ball bowled by the bowler | A van that carries shopping | A way of speaking to a crowd
exercise: Find and copy the word that tells you what the drone carries in «A delivery drone carries a small parcel». | small | drone | *parcel | flies
test: In «So blood is like a delivery service», what is blood being compared to? | A bus driver | A cricket team | *A delivery service | A pair of scissors
test: In «that delivery is pollination», what is the delivery? | Seeds that fall to the ground | *Pollen reaching the carpel in the middle of a flower | A flower being picked for a vase | A bee buzzing past
exam: A shop says «free delivery» on its website. What does this mean? | *The shop will bring your goods to you at no cost | A ball bowled in a game | A shop that sells parcels only | The birth of a new baby at the shop
